WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040
Off a rocky coast, a lighthouse
guides ships safely through the dark.

2
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.480
One more ship sees the
beam at no extra cost.

3
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.430
Ten ships, a hundred ships:

4
00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:13.870
the light shines just as
brightly for all of them.

5
00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.650
Every ship gains.

6
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:18.280
Yet a lighthouse uses resources,

7
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.240
and someone must pay for it.

8
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.500
So who? If everyone
gains from a lighthouse,

9
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.270
why might no one choose to pay for it?

10
00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:29.960
In this mission, you'll sort
goods with two simple tests,

11
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.620
from a sandwich to national defence.

12
00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:34.990
Then you'll put two neighbours in a game:

13
00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:36.420
they both want a flood barrier,

14
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.640
but will either of them pay?

15
00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.210
Your mission: find out
why a good everyone values

16
00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:43.810
can be hard to pay for.
